  "goodToKnow": "Der Gürtel is a belt, and the plural is the same: die Gürtel. The idiom den Gürtel enger schnallen means to tighten your belt, i.e. to save money. In Vienna, der Gürtel is a major ring road, following the line of the former Linienwall fortification. Seat belts are Sicherheitsgurte, from der Gurt, a related word."
